Q: Write a program to Display Pen Details using Class and Objects:
package classobject_pendetails;


class Pen{
    String color;
    String type; //ballpen or gelpen    
    
    //Method for Pen Details
    public void DisplayDetails() {
    System.out.println("Color: " + color);
    System.out.println("Type: " + type);
}
    //Method for Pen Function
    public void Write(){
        System.out.println("Pen Use for Writing Purpose.");
    }
    
}
//Main Class
public class ClassObject_PenDetails {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        //Object for Pen Class
        Pen Pen1=new Pen();
        Pen1.color="Blue";
        Pen1.type="Ball-Pen"; 
        
        //Calling method on the object
        Pen1.DisplayDetails();
        
        //Calling Method for Pen Function
        Pen1.Write();
    } 
}

OUTPUT:
